Feature: Silent guest issuance on first launch
  As a new player
  I want to be playing at once without signing up
  So that nothing stands between me and the first win, and every block still has an account_id to key on

  Background:
    Given the app is configured for tenant "tenant-001"
    And the guest configuration defaults of README section 7 apply
    And AUDIENCE_MODE is "general" and GUEST_ATTESTATION_MODE is "off"
    And the clock is fixed at "2026-10-27T12:00:00Z"

  @happy
  Scenario: First launch creates an account with no screen and no prompt
    Given the device has no credential in secure storage and is online
    When the app starts
    Then no sign-in screen, prompt or permission request is shown
    And the client requests a challenge, solves it and creates the account
    And the response status is 201 with kind "guest" and linked_at null
    And the response carries an account_id, a secret and a session token
    And the secret is stored in secure storage and creation_request_id is deleted from device storage
    And the database holds only the SHA-256 hash of the secret and of the session token

  @happy
  Scenario: A returning guest starts silently
    Given the device holds the secret "device-secret-example-0001" from fixtures/accounts.json
    When the app starts
    Then the client exchanges the secret and the response status is 200
    And no screen is shown
    And accounts.last_active_at for "guest-active" is updated

  @happy
  Scenario: account_id is a stable server-generated UUID that is never taken from a request
    When a creation request body carries an "account_id" field
    Then the field is ignored and the account_id is generated by the server
    And the account_id is a UUID version 4
    And the account_id of an account never changes in any later response

  @edge
  Scenario: A lost response does not create a second account
    Given fixtures/lifecycle-cases.json creation_replay
    When the first creation response is lost and the client retries with the same creation_request_id after 5 minutes
    Then the response status is 201 with the same account_id and a new secret
    And the first secret is retired with reason "rotated"
    And exactly 1 account exists for that creation_request_id

  @edge
  Scenario: A retry after the replay window or after the first exchange is refused
    Given fixtures/lifecycle-cases.json creation_replay
    When the client retries with the same creation_request_id after 20 minutes
    Then the response status is 409 with error "request_consumed"
    And the client runs the normal start with the secret it holds

  @edge
  Scenario: A credential that appears late beats creating a new account
    Given the device starts with no credential and is offline
    And a platform restore delivers a credential to secure storage while the app runs
    When the connection returns
    Then the client reads secure storage once more before creating
    And it exchanges the restored credential and creates no account

  @edge
  Scenario: Offline first launch plays locally and reconciles on first connection
    Given fixtures/lifecycle-cases.json offline_cases with queue_cap 3
    And the device is offline at first launch
    When the player completes tutorial steps s1 and s2 and wins the first level
    Then no screen about identity is shown and nothing is shown as granted by the server
    And the events are queued with a local_event_id and no account_id
    And a fourth event is dropped and counted
    When the network returns and the account is created
    Then the queue is submitted oldest first
    And each receiving block builds its idempotency key from the new account_id and the event facts
    And a rejected event is dropped with its reason and is not retried
    And guest_identity_reconciled reports 3 queued events and 1 dropped event of the cap case

  @edge
  Scenario: Creation retries back off and honour the server
    Given the device is online and the server answers 429 with retry_after_seconds 120
    When the client retries
    Then the first retries follow OFFLINE_CREATE_BACKOFF_SECONDS 5, 30, 120, 600
    And the 429 retry_after_seconds is honoured when it is longer
    And the player sees no error and the game keeps playing

  @edge
  Scenario: Exchange failures show the truth and never create silently
    Given fixtures/accounts.json exchange_cases
    When the client exchanges "device-secret-example-0006" and receives 410 "guest_purged" with reason "inactive"
    Then the welcome-back screen for a purged guest is shown
    And the stored secret is deleted
    And no new guest is created until the player taps "Start a new game"

  @security
  Scenario: Platform web is refused
    When a creation request has platform "web"
    Then the response status is 400 with error "invalid_request"
    And no account is created

  @edge
  Scenario: Mixed audience asks age before any identifier is requested
    Given AUDIENCE_MODE is "mixed" and AGE_THRESHOLD_YEARS is 16
    When the app starts for the first time
    Then the neutral age screen is shown before any request to the server
    And the age screen has no default selection and no hint of a threshold
    And the answer is stored on the device and cannot be changed in the app

  @edge
  Scenario Outline: Under-age outcome in mixed mode
    Given AUDIENCE_MODE is "mixed" and AUDIENCE_UNDER_AGE_ACCOUNT is "<setting>"
    When the player answers with an age below AGE_THRESHOLD_YEARS
    Then <result>

    Examples:
      | setting            | result                                                                                                                  |
      | none               | no request is sent, identity is pending, server-dependent features are hidden, guest_pending_identity has reason under_age |
      | guest_internal_ops | an account is created with age_screen "under_age", no link prompt is ever shown and attestation is not requested        |

  @security
  Scenario: No advertising identifier is read or sent
    When the client creates an account
    Then no advertising identifier appears in any request, header or stored value
